Subject: default C API terminals to grapheme cluster mode

amx reads libghostty-vt cells directly, so a multi-codepoint grapheme cluster
must occupy one cell — DEC private mode 2027. The C API can set the *current*
mode with ghostty_terminal_mode_set, but RIS restores the terminal's default
modes and GhosttyTerminalOptions has no field for those, so clustering is lost
on every full reset. Setting it in Terminal.Options.default_modes makes it both
the initial and the post-reset value.

Vendored base: c5a21edfcbc2d5b46540ad91b7980aca31f5f1f3

diff --git a/vendor/libghostty-vt/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig b/vendor/libghostty-vt/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
--- a/vendor/libghostty-vt/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
+++ b/vendor/libghostty-vt/src/terminal/c/terminal.zig
@@ -343,6 +343,12 @@ fn new_(
         .cols = opts.cols,
         .rows = opts.rows,
         .max_scrollback = opts.max_scrollback,
+
+        // Embedders that read cells directly need DEC mode 2027 so a
+        // multi-codepoint grapheme cluster occupies one cell. Setting it as a
+        // default mode rather than a current mode means RIS restores it; the
+        // C API has no other way to survive a reset.
+        .default_modes = .{ .grapheme_cluster = true },
     });
     errdefer t.deinit(alloc);

